-- courses (08.3-01, COURSE-01, COURSE-02, COURSE-03, COURSE-08, COURSE-09, COURSE-12, COURSE-13;
-- D-400, D-403, D-404, D-406, D-407, D-408, D-409, D-413) — the courses module's eleven tables,
-- their RLS, the `courses` module key and the `lesson` media purpose. GENERATED by drizzle-kit from
-- packages/modules/courses/db/schema.ts, packages/core/db/schema/tenant-modules.ts,
-- packages/core/db/schema/media-assets.ts and packages/contracts/src/{modules,media}.ts; every
-- statement below is drizzle-kit's, unchanged:
--
--   1. the eleven tables with their CHECKs, RLS enabled on each:
--      - `course_categories` (name + cover, unique per tenant ignoring case),
--      - `courses` (the one publication state `draft | published | archived`, D-413; `level`,
--        `outcomes` ≤ 10, `certificate_hours` 0..999 as CHECKs),
--      - `course_modules` and `course_lessons` (ordered, soft-deleted; `requires_previous` D-406 and
--        `is_free` D-407 modeled now; `course_lessons.course_id` denormalised for the gate),
--      - `course_lesson_materials` (ordered `attachment` assets of a lesson),
--      - `course_products` and `course_live_products` (which product opens which course / live;
--        their FKs to `store_products` are hand SQL in the later `*_courses_functions.sql`, MOD-02),
--      - `course_lesson_progress` (PK `(tenant_id, user_id, lesson_id)`, the member's own record,
--        D-408),
--      - `course_tracks`, `course_track_courses` (an ordered path over courses, D-415),
--      - `course_lives` (an agenda entry; `cancelled_at` the only stored state, D-416);
--   2. drop `media_assets_purpose_chk` and `tenant_modules_key_chk`, then (after the FKs and
--      indexes) recreate them ending in 'lesson' (D-409, COURSE-12) and 'courses' (COURSE-01). Both
--      are GENERATED from the contract lists, so appending the values there is what produced them;
--   3. the foreign keys (tenant FKs `on delete cascade`; modules, lessons, materials and links
--      cascade with their parent; `courses.category_id … on delete restrict`, so a category with
--      courses cannot be removed);
--   4. the indexes, every one tenant-first (pgTAP 040), including the partial unique arbiter
--      `course_lessons_tenant_video_uq` (one video asset per LIVE lesson, P22) and the case-
--      insensitive `course_categories_tenant_name_uq` (P13);
--   5. the policies:
--      - every catalogue table: `*_select_tenant` for every lane of the tenant, and
--        `*_insert_admin` / `*_update_admin` / `*_delete_admin` by the `admin_tenant` claim only
--        (D-403, the store's CR-01 posture);
--      - `courses_select_published_or_admin`: a `draft` course is the admin claim's alone — the
--        member read predicate modeled now (D-413); `course_modules_select_tenant` and
--        `course_lessons_select_tenant` follow the course through an `exists` on `public.courses`,
--        `course_lesson_materials_select_lesson` follows the lesson;
--      - `course_lessons_course_gate`, AS RESTRICTIVE (it ANDs with the permissive select; a
--        permissive one would widen access): the admin claim reads every lesson, a member of a
--        locked course reads only its `is_free` lessons. It calls `app.course_locked_ids()` — the
--        kernel stub from `*_course_gate_seam.sql`, which sorts BEFORE this file (RESEARCH
--        Pitfall 2); the store gives it a body in `*_store_course_gate.sql`, which sorts AFTER;
--      - `course_lesson_progress`: select own-or-admin, insert and update `user_id = app.user_id()`
--        only, and NO delete policy (D-408).
--
-- NO BACKFILL: there is no insert into `tenant_modules`. A missing row reads as disabled, which is
-- the module's default (COURSE-01), so for every existing tenant this migration changes nothing a
-- member can observe. Expand-only: no drop table, drop column, rename, set not null or type change;
-- safe to apply before the API revision that calls these objects.

